  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(2)=(63.434\\,9\u2026)^{\u2218}\u2248{63.435}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince ${63.435}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to the nearest integer, is ${x}_{1}={63}^{\u2218}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$\nHence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{\u2218}+x={180}^{\u2218}+{63.435}^{\u2218}\u2248{243}^{\u2218},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={63}^{\u2218}$ and $x={243}^{\u2218}.$",
